        <article class="intropara" style="color:white;">
            <h2>My Top 5 Video Games List</h2>
            <div class="gamecards">
            <section class="gamesection">
                <h2 style="text-align: left;">5. Call Of Duty Modern Warfare 2019</h2>
                <img class="gamelistpics" src="images/Warzone.avif" alt="logo">
                <p>
                    Call of Dutty: Modern Warfare (2019) introduced Call of Duty: Warzone. It was a really popular
                    battle royale where up to 150 players fought across the Verdansk map while a gas circle forced players together.
                    It had unique mechanic like the Gulag which basically gave players a second chance after they died, and teamates
                    could buy them back at buy stations. I include it in my top five games because Warzone was an incredible experience during 
                    lockdown and was a fun way to socialise with friends while being stuck indoors.
                </p>
            </section>
            <section class="gamesection">
                <h2 style="text-align: left;">4. Grand Theft Auto V</h2>
                <img class="gamelistpics" src="images/GTA5.avif" alt="logo">
                <p>
                    Grand Theft Auto V (GTA V) is an open world action game set in the city of Los Santos. Players follow the stories of 
                    three main characters and partake in many missions, heists and world exploration. The game also includes Grand Theft 
                    Auto Online, which lets players play with each other, creating their own characters, stories, and build businesses.
                    I include it in my top five games as this game is endless fun and never gets boring. Playing with friends is a great
                    experience which creates many fun memories.
                </p>
            </section>
            <section class="gamesection">
                <h2 style="text-align: left;">3. Fortnite</h2>
                <img class="gamelistpics" src="images/Fortnite.jpg" alt="logo">
                <p>
                    Fortnite is a popular battle royale game where 100 players drop onto an island, collect weapons and resources and 
                    fight to be the last one standing. The game is unique as it introduces building, constant updates and crossover events 
                    with movies, games and celebrities. I include it in my top five games as Fortnite was such an influencial game in its prime. 
                    Everybody knew about, and played Fortnite. Hopping on with your friends for hours straight after school was a peak experience
                    that is hard to be topped.
                </p>
            </section>
            <section class="gamesection">
                <h2 style="text-align: left;">2. Go Vacation</h2>
                <img class="gamelistpics" src="images/goVacation.webp" alt="logo">
                <p>
                    Go Vacation is an open world game set on a large resort island with different areas like beaches, mountains and cities. Each 
                    of the four parts of the island offer their own set of activies such as racing, water sports, and many more fun mini-games. 
                    I include it in my top five games as Go Vacation for me is driven by pure nostalgia and fun memories. Countless hours were spent
                    with family playing this game and it will always be a classic to me.
                </p>
            </section>
            <section class="gamesection">
                <h2 style="text-align: left;">1. Minecraft</h2>
                <img class="gamelistpics" src="images/Minecraft1.webp" alt="logo">
                <p>
                    Minecraft is a sandbox game where players can explore, build, and survive in a procedurally generated world. You can mine resources,
                    craft tools, build anything and you can do all this with your friends too. I include it in my top five games as Minecraft is peak childhood
                    and it is a game you can always come back to, no matter what age you are. It is my number one game for many reasons, and 
                    <a href="bestgame.html">here's why...</a>
                </p>
            </section>
            </div>
            <section class="lists">
